Integer coefficients for the element routines in this addon.


Base functions (shape functions)
--------------------------------

See file addons/README_basefunctions


List of the coefficients
------------------------

  1-150: all relevant integer coefficients from the stokes & viscoelastic add-on
151-200: reserved for diffuse_interface add-on
201-250: reserved for inertia add-on
251-300: reserved for generalized Stokes add-on
301-350: reserved for compressible_fluid add-on

351  deformation tensor interpolation (in space)

352  deformation tensor interpolation for DG (in age coordinate tau):
     1: P1  2: P2

353  number of intervals N in the age coordinate tau
     NOTE: the age intervals are
         [tau_j,tau_j+1], j=0,...,N-1
       where tau_0=0. The N age points tau_j, j=0,...,N need to be given
       in the array coefficients%ra(1)%a
     NOTE: the number of fields is N*ninttau, where ninttau the number of
       fields within a single interval (ninttau=2 for P1,ninttau=3 for P2).

354  time integration:
     0: default, which is BDF2 (for P1) or BDF3 (for P2) with prediction
        (extrapolated BDF).
     1: Euler explicit/implicit, which should only be used as a first step
        to start the multi-step scheme.
     2: BDF2 with prediction (extrapolated BDF).
     3: BDF3 with prediction (extrapolated BDF).
     NOTE: convection in space is always implicit.

355  spatial discretization:
     0: standard Galerkin
     1: SUPG.

356  The projected velocity gradient tensor (G-method) used for time-integration
     of the deformation gradient tensor is:
     0: Part of the solution vector (DEVSS).
     1: Computed as a separate vector using projection.
     NOTE: this is only relevant for coefficient%i(357)=0.

357  The velocity gradient used for the time integration of the CE for the
     deformation gradient tensor:
     0: The projected velocity gradient tensor (G-method).
        NOTE: for this case coefficient%i(356) determines how the projected
        gradient is supplied to the element routines.
     1: The velocity gradient tensor as derived directly from the velocity.

358  choice parameter in computing a derivative.
     For example coefficient%i(358)=1 means Fxx in dfm_deriv_field.
     See the sources for the possibilities in various derivative routines.

359  choice parameter in computing a derivative.
     For example coefficient%i(359) means the interval number in
     dfm_deriv_field.
     See the sources for the possibilities in various derivative routines.

360  choice parameter in computing a derivative.
     For example coefficient%i(360) means the point (field) number within an
     interval in dfm_deriv_field.
     See the sources for the possibilities in various derivative routines.

361  The location of the solution for the fields in oldvectors.
     This is used in dfm_deriv_field, dfm_deriv_stress_tensor, ... as follows:
       0: solution is in oldvectors%s2 (as used in dfm_elem2)
       1: solution is in oldvectors%s3 (as used in dfm_elem1)
     Setting to this to non-zero is therefore only needed for the legacy
     explicit deformation fields of dfm_elem1.

362  The tau interval (intvaltau) for the implicit part.

363  Type of integral model:
       0: Separable Rivlin-Sawyers
       1: Non-separable Rivlin-Sawyers (not yet available).

364  Spectrum for the separable Rivlin-Sawyers integral model:
       0: discrete spectrum
          NOTE: the moduli G_i and relaxation times lambda_i are given by
                     G_i = coefficients%ra(2)%a(i), i=1,...,n
                lambda_i = coefficients%ra(3)%a(i), i=1,...,n
          where the number of discrete modes n is given by coefficients%i(365)
       1: Mittag-Leffler (not yet available).
       2: Combined discrete spectrum and Carreau (power-law) modes:
           G(t) = sum G_i*exp(-t/lambda_i) + sum G_i/(1+(t/lambda_i)^2)^(n_i/2)

365  The number of modes in the spectrum (for coefficients%i(364)=0 and 2).
     NOTE: setting the coefficients%i(365)=0, the number of modes is set to the
     default value of 1.

366  The damping function(s) for the separable Rivlin-Sawyers integral model:
       0: default=1
       1: h1 = 1, h2 = 0 (UCM model)
       2: h1 = 1/[1+a*(I1-3)], h2 = 0 (used in fractional K-BKZ models)
          NOTE: a=coefficients%r(303)
       3: h1 = alpha/[alpha-3+beta*I1+(1-beta)*I2], h2 = 0 (PSM model)
          NOTE: alpha=coefficients%r(304), beta=coefficients%r(305)

367  The number of discrete modes in the spectrum 2 (coefficients%i(364)=2).
     NOTE: The first coefficients%i(367) number of modes are the discrete ones.
     NOTE: coefficients%i(365) gives the total number of modes.

368  Check for zero velocity and avoid dividing by zero in SUPG.
       0: no
       1: yes
     If a zero velocity is detected in ANY of the integration points of an
     element, the method is switched to using htype=3 and Uscaling=4 with
     Uglobal = coefficient%r(306) in the velocity scaling for ALL integration
     points.
     NOTE: this is a brute force approach to avoid divide by zero, when
           the velocity is exactly zero. It should be used only for that case
           and normally be off.
     NOTE: htype=3 means h is determined by the size of the element:
             2D: h = (elementsize)**0.5
             3D: h = (elementsize)**1/3 (not applicable here)
           hence: h is a constant per element
     NOTE: Uglobal = coefficient%r(306), used in Uscaling=4, must be set to
           a positive value.

369-400 Reserved for future use. Set to zero for future compatibility.

